+---
+title: 'Story 3.4: Terminal Disablement & Narrowly-Scoped Platform Interventions'
+type: 'feature'
+created: '2026-08-19'
+status: 'in-review'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+followup_review_recommended: true
+context: []
+warnings: []
+deferred: []
+baseline_revision: '92d9ed506f70d5ad68626ffeb3791d159c55a266'
+---
+
+<intent-contract>
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** Platform administrators currently have no means to terminally disable end-of-life tenants or perform narrow interventions (like removing a compromised user from an organization) safely. Such actions must be strictly audited and require recent re-authentication, preventing cross-tenant data leakage.
+
+**Approach:** Implement `POST /platform/organizations/:id/terminal-disablement` to transition an organization's access status to `DISABLED` and revoke all its member sessions. Implement `POST /platform/organizations/:id/interventions/remove-member` to remove a specific identity from an organization. Both must enforce recent re-authentication (session age < 15 minutes) and log structured evidence.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- Require recent re-authentication (session created within the last 15 minutes) for these endpoints.
+- Log an `Evidence` record for both actions containing actor, target Organization, target identity (for remove-member), action, and reason.
+- Terminal disablement must invalidate all active sessions for the organization's members.
+- The `DISABLED` state is terminal (no reactivation path in this story).
+- Interventions must be scoped to a single organization (cannot affect other tenants).
+
+**Block If:**
+- The required recent re-authentication threshold is undefined (we will use 15 minutes).
+
+**Never:**
+- Never expose or return general business data in the intervention responses.
+- Never allow these operations without a recorded `reason`.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Terminal Disablement | Valid org, valid reason, recent session | Org accessStatus set to DISABLED, members' sessions deleted, Evidence logged | 401 if session older than 15 mins. 400 if reason missing. |
+| Remove Member Intervention | Valid org, valid member ID, valid reason, recent session | Member removed, Evidence logged | 401 if not recent session. 404 if member not found. |
+
+</intent-contract>
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/platform-organizations.controller.ts` -- Expose terminal disablement and remove member intervention endpoints.
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/platform-organizations.service.ts` -- Implement the business logic for terminal disablement (updating org status, deleting sessions, writing evidence) and remove member (deleting org member, writing evidence).
+- `apps/api/src/modules/access-control/guards/platform-admin.guard.ts` -- Attach `session` to the request object so controllers can verify recent re-authentication.
+- `apps/api/src/common/constants.ts` -- Add new EvidenceActions (`TERMINAL_DISABLEMENT`, `REMOVE_MEMBER_INTERVENTION`).
+
+## Tasks & Acceptance
+
+**Execution:**
+- `apps/api/src/modules/access-control/guards/platform-admin.guard.ts` -- Attach `request.session = session;` along with the identity so the controller can check session age. Update `express.d.ts` if needed (can be handled inline or in types).
+- `apps/api/src/common/constants.ts` -- Add `TERMINAL_DISABLEMENT` and `REMOVE_MEMBER_INTERVENTION` to `EvidenceActions`.
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/dto/terminal-disablement.dto.ts` -- Create DTO requiring `reason` (string, max length, not empty).
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/dto/remove-member-intervention.dto.ts` -- Create DTO requiring `identityId` and `reason`.
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/platform-organizations.service.ts` -- Implement `terminallyDisableOrganization(orgId, reason, actorId)` (transaction: update org `accessStatus` to `DISABLED`, delete sessions for all members, insert Evidence). Implement `removeMemberIntervention(orgId, targetIdentityId, reason, actorId)` (transaction: delete `OrganizationMember`, insert Evidence with target identity in `before`/`after`).
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/platform-organizations.controller.ts` -- Add `POST :id/terminal-disablement` and `POST :id/interventions/remove-member`. In each endpoint handler, verify `req.session.createdAt` is within the last 15 minutes; if not, throw `UnauthorizedException('Recent re-authentication required')`.
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/platform-organizations.controller.spec.ts` -- Add unit tests for recent re-authentication enforcement and endpoint success.
+- `apps/api/src/modules/platform-admin/platform-organizations.service.spec.ts` -- Add unit tests for transactions, session revocation, and evidence logging.
+
+**Acceptance Criteria:**
+- Given an Organization in any lifecycle state, when a Platform Admin with a recently authenticated session submits a terminal disablement with a reason, then the Organization transitions to `DISABLED`, all member access/sessions are immediately revoked, and evidence is committed atomically.
+- Given a Platform Admin with a recently authenticated session, when they submit a narrow remove-member intervention for a target Organization, then the member is removed from that Organization without granting business data access, and an Evidence record includes the target identity.
+- Given an intervention attempt, when the Platform Admin's session is older than 15 minutes, then the server rejects it with an authorization error requiring re-authentication.
